      "writtenOn": "2023-01-09T20:26:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need new static_branch variable instead of (pp_buffer.buffer)?\n\nI thought we could achieve if we move pp_buffer.buffer \u003d kvmalloc_array(xxx) on bottom of init_page_owner?\n\nIs there any race between init_page_pinner and page_pinner_init we need to care?\nI think init_page_pinner function should be called earlier before any __init function so thought there was no race between them.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 409,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 409,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "02da841a21a109383c51663f00f9bed629e48f54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8a0cbfa_39e3d720",
        "filename": "mm/page_pinner.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 409,
      "author": {
        "id": 1904204
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T09:17:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "By the time page_pinner_init() is called, the pp_buffer is already initialized and could be already in use(because page_pinner_inited and failure_tracking are both set) which introduces the race. No?\n\nAnd when pp_buffer is in use, we can\u0027t kfree() the buffer as it might being used. So, I am seting the page_pinner_inited only after it is completely ready to use. And to set this another static variable is defined which tells to the late_init(page_pinner_init) that pp_buffer is properly defined.",
      "parentUuid": "971903aa_2ea81787",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 409,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 409,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "02da841a21a109383c51663f00f9bed629e48f54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73ab328c_2ebc22de",
        "filename": "mm/page_pinner.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 409,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275554
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T17:03:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I meant was let\u0027s make it ready(i.e., page_pinner_inited set) once everything set up. What we lose is miss cma allocation failure during the init phase of drivers but I think that would be rare unless there is clear bug.\n \n```\ndiff --git a/mm/page_pinner.c b/mm/page_pinner.c\nindex 2567206e7ce8..5cfceb361e2c 100644\n--- a/mm/page_pinner.c\n+++ b/mm/page_pinner.c\n@@ -99,7 +99,6 @@ static void init_page_pinner(void)\n        pp_buffer.index \u003d 0;\n \n        register_failure_stack();\n-       static_branch_enable(\u0026page_pinner_inited);\n }\n \n struct page_ext_operations page_pinner_ops \u003d {\n@@ -403,24 +402,24 @@ static int __init page_pinner_init(void)\n {\n        struct dentry *pp_debugfs_root;\n \n-       if (!static_branch_unlikely(\u0026page_pinner_inited))\n-               return 0;\n-\n-       pr_info(\"page_pinner enabled\\n\");\n+       if (page_pinner_enabled \u0026\u0026 pp_buffer.buffer) {\n+               pp_debugfs_root \u003d debugfs_create_dir(\"page_pinner\", NULL);\n \n-       pp_debugfs_root \u003d debugfs_create_dir(\"page_pinner\", NULL);\n+               debugfs_create_file(\"buffer\", 0444,\n+                               pp_debugfs_root, NULL,\n+                               \u0026proc_buffer_operations);\n \n-       debugfs_create_file(\"buffer\", 0444,\n-                           pp_debugfs_root, NULL,\n-                           \u0026proc_buffer_operations);\n+               debugfs_create_file(\"failure_tracking\", 0644,\n+                               pp_debugfs_root, NULL,\n+                               \u0026failure_tracking_fops);\n \n-       debugfs_create_file(\"failure_tracking\", 0644,\n-                           pp_debugfs_root, NULL,\n-                           \u0026failure_tracking_fops);\n+               debugfs_create_file(\"buffer_size\", 0644,\n+                               pp_debugfs_root, NULL,\n+                               \u0026buffer_size_fops);\n+               static_branch_enable(\u0026page_pinner_inited);\n+               pr_info(\"page_pinner enabled\\n\");\n+       }\n \n-       debugfs_create_file(\"buffer_size\", 0644,\n-                           pp_debugfs_root, NULL,\n-                           \u0026buffer_size_fops);\n        return 0;\n }\n late_initcall(page_pinner_init)\n\n```",
      "parentUuid": "e8a0cbfa_39e3d720",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 409,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 409,
        "endChar": 49
